I'm not going to explain this anymore.

01:09:19.720 --> 01:09:22.700
We're pretty much at that point now where you guys know what's going on.

01:09:22.820 --> 01:09:23.940
Is it essential today?

01:09:24.120 --> 01:09:25.160
Not in 1986.

01:09:25.720 --> 01:09:29.360
Or I think this game came out in 85, 84 in Japan.

01:09:30.040 --> 01:09:32.200
So we're talking about 86, though, because it's NES.

01:09:32.280 --> 01:09:33.660
See, I'm already explaining it too much, guys.

01:09:33.840 --> 01:09:34.640
So take it away, Sean.

01:09:34.800 --> 01:09:36.120
Is this game essential?

01:09:36.780 --> 01:09:40.280
I think that this game is a boatload of fun to play.

01:09:40.480 --> 01:09:42.560
I think that it has a lot of value.

01:09:43.080 --> 01:09:46.940
I don't think that anything has really been lost over time.

01:09:47.080 --> 01:09:56.780
It's the best scrolling game that we've played in terms of, like, whether it's a top-down or a sideways, like, I hated 1942.

01:09:58.060 --> 01:10:02.600
I didn't really like Commando, if you want to consider this a part of the same genre.

01:10:02.600 --> 01:10:08.040
I think this really showed what this genre can be on a home computer system.

01:10:09.500 --> 01:10:14.740
And I think that it's legacy and just how fun it still is to play.

01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:17.680
I think it's a – I'm going to rate it essential.

01:10:18.860 --> 01:10:21.760
Wow. We have one essential vote.

01:10:21.920 --> 01:10:25.420
There's three of us, so we need two to put it in there.

01:10:25.780 --> 01:10:27.640
Joe. All right.

01:10:27.740 --> 01:10:30.280
I might get a little long-winded here, so everybody settle in.

01:10:30.300 --> 01:10:31.900
I'll settle in. So get a drink if you want.

01:10:33.520 --> 01:10:39.120
So first of all, this kind of scrolling shmup is not usually my kind of game.

01:10:40.080 --> 01:10:46.800
So it's been hard for me to judge this one, and I was – you know, I've got a lot of back and forth in my head up until, like, in this session.

01:10:46.940 --> 01:10:48.300
I mean, I was still thinking about it.

01:10:49.600 --> 01:10:51.000
But I think the game's beautiful.

01:10:51.000 --> 01:10:59.160
It's got a really great design, and it's one of the better, like, looking and feeling games of this genre that we've played so far.

01:10:59.300 --> 01:11:06.280
But maybe, like, of this genre that I've ever played, like, one of the better feeling games to me.

01:11:07.280 --> 01:11:15.240
And I think somebody who enjoys this kind of game in general would really love this game, probably more so than I did.

01:11:15.460 --> 01:11:21.380
But I don't know if it's something that I personally would frequently be like, I want to go back and play that again.

01:11:21.600 --> 01:11:31.220
But, like, while I'm playing it, like, I can – I can understand that there might be someone out there that doesn't like platformers.

01:11:31.220 --> 01:11:33.320
